# Environment + secrets
#
# Belt and braces: wildcard all dotenv variants, named secret files,
# and common key/cert extensions. Keeps accidental secret commits
# (like tunnel tokens, OAuth creds, DB passwords, bootstrapping
# service accounts) out of git regardless of what naming convention
# a contributor picks. `.env.example` is allowed back in by the
# negation pattern — it's the only dotenv file that should be
# committed, and it must never contain real values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.secret
*.secrets
secrets/
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml

# Credentials / keys
*.key
*.pem
*.crt
*.cert
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*_rsa
*_ed25519
*_ecdsa
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
id_ecdsa*

# Cloud & tunnel provider creds
.cloudflared/
cert.pem
*-credentials.json

